course: dictionary
lesson: 5574
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show which one you need. Letting is a good example. «Mum is letting me stay up late» means she is allowing me to do something.
explain: Letting something happen can also mean not stopping it, as in «letting the water run». Ask yourself: is someone giving permission, or is something just being allowed to continue?
explain: Context clues help you choose. In «A red face and sweat are the body letting heat out», letting out means releasing heat, so the body is allowing heat to escape. Try your meaning in the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
explain: Letting also appears in phrases like letting go, letting off steam and letting someone down. In British English, letting a house or flat means renting it out to someone. Read the whole sentence before you decide which meaning is right.
fact: Letting is the present participle of let: let, lets, let, letting.
fact: «Letting» can mean allowing someone to do something, as in «Mum is letting me stay up late».
fact: Letting something happen means not stopping it, such as letting the water run.
fact: In British English, letting a house or flat means renting it out to someone.
fact: «A red face and sweat are the body letting heat out»: here letting means releasing heat, and dizziness or feeling sick means stop and tell an adult.
exercise: «Mum is letting me stay up late.» What does letting mean here? | *Allowing me to stay up | Hitting me | Losing my way | Stopping me from sleeping
exercise: «A red face and sweat are the body letting heat out.» What does letting mean here? | Stopping the heat from escaping | Making new heat | Hiding the heat | *Releasing the heat so it escapes
exercise: What does «letting someone down» mean? | Waking someone up | Lending someone money | Helping someone up | *Disappointing someone
test: In British English, what does «letting a flat» mean? | Leaving the flat empty forever | Painting the walls | Cleaning the flat | *Renting the flat out to someone
test: A safety rule says never «letting strangers into the house». What does it mean? | Lending strangers the house keys | Letting strangers out of the house | Telling strangers the time | *Allowing strangers to come in
exam: Which sentence uses letting to mean not stopping something? | Mum is letting me go to the park | Letting go of the rope now | *Please stop letting the tap run, the water is being wasted | I am letting off steam after school
